 Q: What’s the difference between rolling update and recreate strategy in Kubernetes?
ANS: RollingUpdate gradually updates pods without downtime and is the default strategy.
Recreate stops all pods before creating new ones, causing downtime but ensuring no overlap between old and new versions.
| Feature         | RollingUpdate               | Recreate                                 |
| --------------- | --------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| Downtime        | No                          | Yes                                      |
| Pod replacement | Gradual, one-by-one         | All old pods stopped first               |
| Use case        | Most production deployments | Single-instance or incompatible versions |
